   --- SOVEREIGN RECIPROCAL COMMONS RIDER (SRCL-1.0) ---

   Section 10. Express Conditions Precedent (Jacobsen v. Katzer Doctrine)
   All permissions, grants, and licenses conferred by this document are subject
   to the express conditions precedent set forth in Sections 11, 12, and 13.
   Any use, reproduction, preparation of Derivative Works, distribution, or
   AI Training outside of or in breach of these conditions is unpermitted,
   void ab initio, and constitutes willful copyright infringement under 17 U.S.C.
   § 106 and § 501.

   Section 11. Reciprocal Engine Source Transparency (Modified Core Runtime Clause)
   Commercial use, monetization, deployment, and operation of this Work are
   expressly authorized and welcomed for all individuals and enterprises.
   You are fully permitted to build proprietary applications, offer hosted services,
   embed compiled object binaries, and monetize software incorporating this Work
   under the LLVM Exception without any obligation to disclose or license your
   independent application source code or proprietary service code.

   Supremacy of the LLVM Exception for Applications: For the avoidance of doubt,
   the LLVM Exception governs all independent application code, user services,
   client modules, proprietary algorithms, and composite executables that compile,
   link against, or embed the Object form of this Work. Linking against this Work,
   compiling it into a proprietary service binary, or communicating with this
   Work over network protocols imposes zero obligation to provide or license
   source code for your independent application or service.

   Limited Reciprocity for Direct Engine Modifications: The reciprocal source
   transparency requirement of this Section 11 applies exclusively to direct
   modifications, forks, or alterations made to the core Source code files of
   this Work itself. Only if You directly modify the Source code files of this
   Work and deploy such modified core runtime as a public or commercial networked
   SaaS or API service, You must make the Source code of Your modifications to
   this Work publicly available under these same license terms within thirty (30)
   days of deployment.

   Section 12. Reciprocal AI Weight Release ($25M Frontier AI Anti-Enclosure Covenant)
   (a) Nature of Covenant, Scope, and Definitions: This Section operates both as an
       express condition precedent under copyright law and as an independent,
       binding contractual covenant governing access, ingestion, and computational
       utilization of this Work. The covenants herein are contractual terms of
       access and use that bind any Qualifying Enterprise irrespective of whether
       AI Training is held to constitute a derivative work, fair use, or non-infringing
       computational activity under copyright law.
       For the purposes of this Section:
       (i) "AI Training" means using the Source code, Object code, architectural
           specifications, internal reasoning traces, documentation, test suites,
           prompts, or embedded training datasets of this Work to train, pre-train,
           fine-tune, distill, align, optimize, or reinforce any neural network,
           machine learning model, or generative foundation model.
       (ii) "Model Weights" means all learned numerical parameters, tensors,
           biases, checkpoint files, embedding layers, and tokenizer definitions
           governing inference.
       (iii) "Qualifying Enterprise" means any commercial enterprise, corporation,
           conglomerate, foundation AI research laboratory, or affiliated Legal
           Entity with annual gross revenues, aggregate raised investment capital,
           or balance-sheet valuation exceeding twenty-five million United States
           Dollars ($25,000,000 USD).

   (b) Condition of Weight Release: If a Qualifying Enterprise conducts AI
       Training upon this Work or its Derivative Works, it is an express condition
       precedent of this License that such Qualifying Enterprise must publish and
       release the resulting Model Weights, architecture specifications, and
       inference recipes openly to the general public under an OSI-approved open
       source license or permissive OpenRAIL or Apache-compatible license within
       thirty (30) days of commercial availability, internal production use, or
       public release.

   (c) Safe Harbor for Builders, Researchers, and Startups: Individual developers,
       open-source collaborators, academic institutions, non-profit organizations,
       and commercial enterprises with annual gross revenues and capital below
       twenty-five million United States Dollars ($25,000,000 USD) are explicitly
       exempt from this Model Weight release condition.

   (d) Anti-Circumvention and Intermediary Scope: The obligations of this Section 12
       bind: (i) any Qualifying Enterprise; (ii) any parent, subsidiary, affiliate,
       joint venture, or successor entity; (iii) any contractor, subcontractor,
       research partner, agent, or third party conducting AI Training for the direct
       or indirect benefit of, under contract with, funded by, or transferring
       resulting Model Weights or training artifacts to a Qualifying Enterprise; and
       (iv) any entity that transfers, assigns, licenses, or provides resulting Model
       Weights to a Qualifying Enterprise. No Qualifying Enterprise may evade this
       condition through intermediaries, contract training, synthetic distillation
       relays, or subsidiary entities.

   (e) Automatic License Forfeiture: Failure of a Qualifying Enterprise (or any party
       acting on its behalf under subsection (d)) to satisfy the condition in
       subsection (b) results in immediate, automatic, and retroactive termination
       of all copyright, patent, and trademark licenses granted herein. Any continued
       reproduction, distribution, inference hosting, or commercial utilization of
       models or software derived from such training constitutes willful copyright
       infringement under Title 17 of the United States Code.

   Section 13. Dual Remedies: Statutory Copyright Damages and Contractual Covenants
   (a) Copyright Remedy: Any Qualifying Enterprise or party that conducts
       unauthorized AI Training on this Work in breach of Section 12 acts without a
       license, committing willful copyright infringement subject to maximum
       statutory damages of up to one hundred fifty thousand United States Dollars
       ($150,000 USD) per infringed work pursuant to 17 U.S.C. § 504(c)(2),
       disgorgement of profits, and permanent injunctive relief under 17 U.S.C. § 502.

   (b) Contractual Alternative and Agreed Licensing Fee: In the event any court of
       competent jurisdiction determines that AI Training on this Work does not
       constitute copyright infringement or falls within affirmative defenses such
       as fair use, accessing, downloading, ingesting, parsing, or executing this
       Work constitutes affirmative assent to this License as a binding bilateral
       contract. Any Qualifying Enterprise that breaches Section 12 agrees to pay
       to Licensor, as liquidated damages and an agreed reasonable commercial licensing
       fee, the greater of: (i) one hundred fifty thousand United States Dollars
       ($150,000 USD) per work ingested; or (ii) ten percent (10%) of all gross
       revenues realized by the Qualifying Enterprise from the commercialization,
       operation, or API deployment of the resulting model or service, in addition
       to restitution for unjust enrichment.

   Section 14. Prevailing Party Legal Fees and Costs
   In any legal proceeding, arbitration, or judicial action brought to enforce
   the terms of this License, for copyright infringement arising from breach
   of the conditions precedent herein, or for breach of contract, the prevailing
   party shall be entitled to an award of its reasonable attorney fees, expert
   witness fees, and litigation costs pursuant to 17 U.S.C. § 505 and applicable law.

   Section 15. Severability and Preservation of Grant
   If any provision, sentence, or clause of this Rider is held invalid, illegal,
   or unenforceable by a court of competent jurisdiction, such invalidity shall
   not affect any other provision of this License. The remaining provisions
   shall remain in full legal force and effect, and the invalid clause shall be
   reformed to the minimum extent necessary to achieve its economic intent.

   Section 16. Governing Law and Exclusive Venue
   This License, and all claims or causes of action arising out of or related to
   this Work or License, shall be governed by and construed in accordance with
   the federal laws of the United States of America and the substantive laws of
   the State of Texas, without giving effect to conflict of laws principles.
   Any judicial action, proceeding, or litigation shall be brought exclusively in
   the United States District Court for the Western District of Texas (Austin
   Division), and each party irrevocably submits to the personal and subject-matter
   jurisdiction of such court.
